  "arrangerNotes": "Verse (16 bars), vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1878 J. F. Perry & Co. sheet music (page images from the New York Public Library's public IIIF service and the LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key A flat major, 4/4. Melody only: the 1878 lyrics are written in minstrel dialect, so the tune is given without words. No simplification needed (no notes outside the key). Range low 5 to 5; C and D arrangements are the same notes. The song was Virginia's state song from 1940 to 1997, when it was retired because of its lyrics (Wikipedia, 'Carry Me Back to Old Virginny'). C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
  "verified": true
}
